From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gdi32: Uniscribe range features by range; alternates by lParameter

ScriptShapeOpenType and ScriptPlaceOpenType with several ranges (rcRangeChars, rpRangeProperties) apply each range's features to its own characters: a substitution feature's lookups run only at the glyphs whose cluster begins in a range that has it on (its own record, else the script's defaults), a positioning feature on in some ranges only gives the other ranges' glyphs their advances and offsets back. Before, the first range's features were used for the whole run. An alternate substitution takes the feature record's lParameter as the 1-based index of the alternate (one beyond the set leaves the glyph); it always took the first.
